module

public import Theory.GroupTheory.Amalgam.FiniteTwists
public import Mathlib.Data.Fin.VecNotation

/-!
# Published coordinates for the full binary G₂ twist calculation

Positive words in `(CEF, FS, C)` and `(CEF, ER, C)` label 192 rows on each
side. The 64 overlap rows use `(CEF, C, E)`. Products and the two embeddings
are recorded literally; matrix labels retain all 64 binary entries.

This is data, with no group realization or completeness assertion. The two
independent proof obligations are `table.Realization concreteAmalgam` and
`table.TwistsVerified`. Their combination constructs endpoint automorphisms
by `FiniteTable.Realization.factorsThrough`.

The reproducible `source/generate.py` uses the ATLAS root conventions and
license: Gerald Höhn and the ATLAS contributors, ATLAS Research and
Attribution License 1.0, LICENSES/ATLAS.txt. Source application:
Aschbacher--Smith F.1.12(I)(3), at q = 2, printed pp.262--263.
-/

